\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.20}{\ignorespaces \xpg@aux {}{french}Stack overflow. The way in which space in the stack is allocated is shown on the left. (Notice that by convention the stack is drawn with the top of the stack at the bottom---so the stack ``grows'' downwards.) On the right three situations are shown: a. Normal operation. Only a part of the local buffer has been used. b. Critical situation: The buffer is completely full. c. Stack Overflow: The buffer is overfull and the return address has been overwritten.}}{297}{figure.8.20}\protected@file@percent }
